      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "RFC: Claws",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- Defines Claws as starter setup manifests for runnable OpenClaw agent setups.\n- Keeps Claws distinct from plugin-bundled skills and RFC 0009 feeds while reusing feeds for discovery/curation.\n- Documents the authored OpenClaw stack through export, skills, MCP, doctor diagnostics, and the two authored update/reconcile PRs.\n- Keeps connector installers out of the first-series plan; connectors remain preview-only/fail-closed until OpenClaw has a connector-owned setup surface.\n- Keeps ClawHub and automation as separate follow-up tracks.\n\n## Current OpenClaw Stack\n\n1. openclaw/openclaw#101328: validation lifecycle\n2. openclaw/openclaw#101755: consent-gated apply and artifact provenance\n3. openclaw/openclaw#101973: workspace/persona apply\n4. openclaw/openclaw#102228: plugin artifact installers and uninstall warnings\n5. openclaw/openclaw#102296: status/remove lifecycle\n6. openclaw/openclaw#102306: export authoring\n7. openclaw/openclaw#102383: skill artifacts\n8. openclaw/openclaw#102406: MCP artifacts\n9. openclaw/openclaw#102427: doctor diagnostics\n10. openclaw/openclaw#102959: update planning and reconcile preview\n11. openclaw/openclaw#102982: consent-gated update apply\n\n## Separate Follow-Up Tracks\n\n- openclaw/clawhub: schema/data model, publish validation/docs, search/detail/API, feed export and published E2E.\n- openclaw/openclaw automation: automation preview, one consent-gated automation substrate, automation provenance/status, disable/remove E2E.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `git diff --check`\n- Manual RFC consistency scan for update/reconcile, connector, ClawHub, and automation staging language\r\n",
